  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are trying to create an array AAA containing NNN integers. However, your array-creating-machine has some restrictions. More formally, you are given a constant DDD, and two arrays BBB and CCC, each with MMM elements, then:\n\n\nAi≤DA_i \\le DAi​≤D for all 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N\nAi≥Ai−1A_i \\ge A_{i - 1}Ai​≥Ai−1​ for all 1&lt;i≤N1 \\lt i \\le N1&lt;i≤N\nACj⋅Bj≤DA_{C_j}\\cdot B_j \\le DACj​​⋅Bj​≤D for all 1≤j≤M1 \\le j \\le M1≤j≤M\nFind how many different arrays can you create. Since answer can be big, print it modulo\n998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT - the number of test cases. The test cases then follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains 333 integers NNN, MMM, and DDD - the length of the array AAA you need to create, the length of BBB and CCC, the constant from the statement.\nThe iii-th line of the next MMM lines of each test case contains two integers CiC_iCi​ and BiB_iBi​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case output a single integer - the number of different arrays you can create modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^{4}1≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1071 \\le N \\le 10^71≤N≤107",
      "1≤M,D≤1051 \\le M, D \\le 10^51≤M,D≤105",
      "1≤Ci≤N1 \\le C_i \\le N1≤Ci​≤N",
      "1≤Bi≤D1 \\le B_i \\le D1≤Bi​≤D",
      "It's guaranteed that the sum of MMM over all test cases doesn't exceed 10510^5105, and sum of DDD over all test cases doesn't exceed 10510^5105",
      "It's guaranteed that in each test case all CiC_iCi​ are different",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 111 (30 points)**: sum of DDD over all test cases doesn't exceed 300030003000.",
      "**Subtask 222 (70 points)**: Original constraints."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
